    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=30^\\circ,\\ 210^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x\\cos30^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin30^\\circ&=\\sin x\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cos x-\\frac12\\sin x&=\\sin x\\\\\\sqrt3\\cos x&=3\\sin x\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $\\cos x=0$, the last equation is not satisfied. Divide by $3\\cos x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan x&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\\\x&=30^\\circ,\\ 210^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
